---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="About"
      description="Blackwood Intelligence conducts forensic analysis of systems, incentives, and structural failure."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>

      <h1 class="sr-only">About — Blackwood Intelligence</h1>

      <hr class="heavy" style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 3rem;" />

      <!-- Opening -->
      <div class="about-opening">
        <p class="about-lead">
          Blackwood Intelligence conducts forensic analysis of systems, incentives, and structural failure.
        </p>
        <p class="about-sub">
          Our work focuses on how organizations, markets, and institutions behave under pressure,
          particularly when incentives, information flow, and operational reality begin diverging.
        </p>
        <p class="about-sub">
          Blackwood operates independently and publishes analysis exploring collapse dynamics,
          systemic adaptation, and strategic uncertainty across complex environments.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Dossier sections -->
      <div class="about-body">

        <div class="about-row">
          <span class="about-row__label">Positioning</span>
          <div class="about-row__content">
            <p>Blackwood is a small independent research desk.</p>
            <p>Some work is published publicly through Analysis, Anatomy, and Signals.
            Other conversations remain private.</p>
            <p>The objective is not commentary, prediction theater, or narrative alignment.
            The objective is structural clarity: understanding how systems behave when pressure
            exceeds the assumptions holding them together.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-row">
          <span class="about-row__label">Method</span>
          <div class="about-row__content">
            <p>Analysis begins with structural questions rather than conclusions.</p>
            <p>Each piece traces incentives, constraints, dependencies, and information flow
            to identify where systems become inconsistent with their apparent design.</p>
            <p>Where evidence is incomplete, uncertainty is stated explicitly rather than
            concealed behind certainty.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-row">
          <span class="about-row__label">Signals</span>
          <div class="about-row__content">
            <p>Signals record shorter observations: early indicators, structural tensions,
            asymmetries, and emerging anomalies that may not yet justify full analysis.</p>
            <p>Some signals remain isolated. Others later develop into larger structural failures.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-row">
          <span class="about-row__label">Situations We Examine</span>
          <div class="about-row__content">
            <p>Blackwood takes on situations where the prevailing explanation no longer adequately accounts for what is happening.</p>
            <p>This may include:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Contested decisions.</strong> Multiple actors operate under conflicting interests, rights, or constraints, and the consequences of their choices extend beyond any single party.</li>
              <li><strong>Failed interventions.</strong> A strategy, restructuring, policy, or corrective measure fails to achieve its stated objective, or produces consequences that undermine it.</li>
              <li><strong>Structural contradictions.</strong> An organisation, institution, or market behaves in ways that its stated incentives, assumptions, or objectives cannot adequately explain.</li>
              <li><strong>Asymmetric positions.</strong> Formal authority, information, economic exposure, and practical control are distributed unevenly, making conventional assessments of power or vulnerability incomplete.</li>
              <li><strong>Unusual situations.</strong> An event, pattern, or emerging problem resists familiar explanations, and understanding its underlying mechanism could materially change how it is approached.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We are not limited to a particular industry. The relevant question is whether the situation contains a structural problem worth examining.</p>
            <p>Selected cases may be considered for independent analysis or private research engagements.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-row">
          <span class="about-row__label">Working With Blackwood</span>
          <div class="about-row__content">
            <p>We welcome enquiries about situations that could benefit from an independent examination, whether the question is already clear or still taking shape.</p>
            <p>You can reach us with a brief description of the situation and what you'd like us to look into. We'll take it from there.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-row">
          <span class="about-row__label">Private Enquiries</span>
          <div class="about-row__content">
            <p>Private enquiries are handled separately from our published research, and any materials shared for a potential engagement remain private unless permission is granted. For initial enquiries, it is best to hold off on sending confidential or restricted documents so any specific confidentiality needs can be discussed first.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-row about-row--contact">
          <span class="about-row__label">Contact</span>
          <div class="about-row__content">
            <p>To discuss a situation:</p>
            <div class="about-contact-links">
              <a href="mailto:analysis@blackwoodintel.com">analysis@blackwoodintel.com</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /* ── Opening block ── */
  .about-opening {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .about-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .about-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .about-sub:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* ── Dossier grid ── */
  .about-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .about-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    padding: 1.75rem 0 2rem;
  }

  /* ── Row label ── */
  .about-row__label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  /* ── Row content ── */
  .about-row__content p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 0.9875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 0.9em;
  }

  .about-row__content p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-row__content ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 0.9em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .about-row__content li {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 0.9875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gray-200);
  }

  /* ── Engagements list ── */
  .about-engagement-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 0.9em 0;
  }

  .about-engagement-list li {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 0.9875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    padding-left: 1em;
    position: relative;
  }

  .about-engagement-list li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* ── Contact ── */
  .about-contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .about-contact-links a {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    width: fit-content;
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .about-contact-links a:hover {
    color: var(--black);
    border-bottom-color: var(--black);
  }

  /* ── Mobile ── */
  @media (max-width: 580px) {
    .about-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      padding: 1.5rem 0 1.75rem;
    }

    .about-row__label {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
